            "review_title": "Review at Menya Yoshino Shoten Da Nang",
            "review_text": "1926yanks\nSeattle, Washington755 contributions\n0\nGreat Little Ramen Place\nNov 2025 • Friends\nThis is a small restaurant on a side street in Da Nang. It has 2-3 tables for two & 8-10 counter seats, overlooking the narrow kitchen area. \nMy friend & went here on a stormy night & had the perfect soup meal. The ramen noodles can be ordered two way, & the broth is chicken-based, almost creamy in consistency. We also had some delicious pan-fried gyoza. \nI’ve been here before & enjoy sitting on the counter. There also are some Japanese whiskeys, served straight up or with soda. \nTasty, inexpensive meal. The bowl of broth w/noodles costs less than $8US. There are a few ramen soups to choose from.\nRead more\nWritten November 19, 2025",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-04",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
